><surname>Yahagi</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Fushiya</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Protective effect of (+)-catechin against 5-fluorouracil-induced myelosuppression in mice</article-title><source>Toxicology</source><year>2004</year><volume>201</volume><fpage>133</fpage><lpage>42</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15297028</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brecher</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Schneiderman</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A time-saving device for the counting of reticulocytes</article-title><source>Am J Clin Pathol</source><year>1950</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>1079</fpage><lpage>83</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14783090</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Takano</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Tanaka</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsukamoto</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Yahagi</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Fushiya</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Isolation of (+)-catechin and (-)-epicatechin from <italic>Actinidia arguta</italic> as bone marrow cell proliferation promoting compounds</article-title><source>Planta Med</source><year>2003</year><volume>69</volume><fpage>321</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12709898</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Clark</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name><name><surname>Kamen</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The human hematopoietic colony-stimulating factors</article-title><source>Science</source><year>1987</year><volume>236</volume><fpage>1229</fpage><lpage>37</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3296190</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mangi</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>Newland</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Interleukin-3 in hematology and oncology: current state of knowledge and future directions</article-title><source>Cytokines Cell Mol Ther</source><year>1999</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>87</fpage><lpage>95</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10515681</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kakiuchi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kobayshi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Satomi</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Miura</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Kasahara</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Kondo</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Flow cytometric analysis of erythropoietic abnormality: changes in the cell maturity index of reticulocytes and retic distribution index are useful as indicators of erythropoietic toxicity in non-clinical studies</article-title><source>J Toxicol Sci</source><year>2006</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>111</fpage><lpage>22</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16772701</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fujii</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Imamura</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Han</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hashin